{
  "id": "Lyo.RequestSigning",
  "name": "Lyo.RequestSigning",
  "area": "Security",
  "tagline": "Timestamped HMAC request signatures. The HMAC key comes from configuration.",
  "description": "Header Lyo-Signature is t=<unix seconds>,v1=<lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256>. v1 is the canonicalization scheme. Sign with Key. Verify accepts Key and, when set, PreviousKey. The default max age is 5 minutes. A timestamp exactly on the boundary is still valid.",
  "features": [
    "**Canonical lines are v1, the unix time, the method, the scheme, the host, the path and query, and the body hash.** The host is the host the request reports. No port is added or stripped.",
    "**A DelegatingHandler adds the header on outbound HttpRequestMessage.** The HMAC key is the UTF-8 bytes of Key."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddRequestSigning(o => o.Key = configuration[\"RequestSigning:Key\"]!);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [],
  "links": [],
